    {
      "id": "claim_06f83a1f3491408d8cc3f4ffb379833e",
      "statement": "`user.updated` routes back through `upsertProfileFromClerkUser`, whose existing-profile path re-attempts the invitation membership insert; without it a membership insert that failed on `user.created` would be permanent because the webhook still answered 200 and Clerk never retried.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/api/webhooks/clerk/route.ts#L28-L49",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:617ff80b3a755ee1177647af4ad450e53abc682a3674961c0de79d57bf8f09fe:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://modules/auth/data/provisioning.ts#L73-L88",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:387036ea826e2a9d78b107bdcad82e400d4e0eb3883ad7b17756160125695d15:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_d59c40ec5d104d408c44311ef36e1627",
      "statement": "Provisioning runs only on the service-role client because no Clerk session exists for `user.created`/`user.deleted`, making the Clerk webhook route the sole sanctioned `service_role` path (rule 3); a throw becomes a 500 so Clerk retries, and any future caller outside that route would be running with RLS bypassed.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/api/webhooks/clerk/route.ts#L46-L49",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:01a361b0e7db0501059030afcf2056c9a45fbf195b61a5117232980cf84d3763:"
